other cps call within the previous cps call, not the outside.

f x (\r -> g r \r2 -> h r2) is CPS
not
f x (\r -> g r) (\r2 -> ...) (\r3 -> ...)

the CPS \r -> k r itself is a Cont r a = (a->r)->r which contain a continuation k :: a -> r

\r -> k r is CPS is Cont r a
k :: a->r is continuation k

when k is unary \r -> k r is equal to k by eta conversion
when k is binary, \r -> k r \r2 -> ..., k r \r2 -> ... is CPS, is Cont r a

use \r1 -> g r1 \r2 -> ... to chain all CPS in one lambda, even use >>=

pyth_m :: Float -> Float -> Cont a Float
pyth_m a b = pow2_m a >>= (\a2 ->
             (pow2_m b >>= (\b2 ->
             (cont (add' a2 b2) >>= (\anb ->
             (cont (sqrt' anb) >>= (\r ->
             return r)))))
